  "content": "12 stranded backpackers rescued from Langtang\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nTuesday, October 7, 2025\n0\nComments\nRasuwa, October 7\nTwelve trekkers stranded in the Langtang region have been safely rescued by the Nepali Army and other security agencies.\nAmong the 16 trekkers from Bhaktapur, four went missing in the flood, and the remaining were safely rescued by the Nepali Army, Nepal Police, and the Armed Police Force Nepal. They were brought to Syaphrubesi after the rescue.\nThe police have said that those rescued have all been sent to Kathmandu. Bhaktapur residents Sanskriti Shrestha, Kisan Shrestha, Sangita Shrestha and Ravi Shrestha, who were on the Langtang trek, are missing since Saturday.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nElection Commission\nshare market\nGen Z\nlichhibari land scam\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nRSS is a government-run national news portal of Nepal.\nMore From the Author\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nBody of missing tourist in Langtang found\n11 months ago\nFrench trekker dies in Rasuwa\n2 years ago\nKyanjin valley in Langtang is waiting for you for the best adventure experience\n5 years ago\nSlugging it out on two wheels: the Langtang ride I\n6 years ago\nFrench national dies after Langtang trek\n7 years ago\nAn ambassador’s journey to Nepal’s mountains\n7 years ago\nMost Read\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\nCAA publishes domestic airfare rates, Kathmandu–Dhangadhi at Rs 17,579\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nDeath toll from landslides and floods rises to 52 across Nepal\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nPolitics\nElection Commission invites parties for talks on upcoming House election\n17 hours ago\nSociety\nSeven charged in Pokhara Lichhibari land scam involving former ministers and officials\n17 hours ago\nOpinion\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\n24 hours ago\nBlog\nWhen Nepal’s youth dared to dream of a better tomorrow\n2 days ago\nSociety\nAI and fake accounts drove one third of online buzz during Nepal Gen Z uprising\n2 days ago",
